; Stage 15 W9 defect 21: a single-method protocol declared inside a NAMESPACE,
; so a consumer in another namespace must spell it `dp/Describe`.
;
; The conforming type, its method, and the `extend` all live here and reference
; the protocol BARE — the "a reference from inside its own namespace" half of the
; namespaced-protocol rule. The consumer (examples/w9-dyn-ns.nuc) spells the same
; protocol qualified and boxes into `(dyn dp/Describe)`; both must land on the one
; identity `dp/Describe`.
;
; Boxing deliberately happens in the consumer, not here — the file stays a pure
; single-protocol library. (It is no longer forced: until Stage 15 B2b a file
; with an explicit `(ns …)` could not reach `default-allocator` at all, because
; `scope-lookup` qualified a bare global key with the current namespace and had
; no fallback. `globals-lookup-ref` now falls back to the flattened set and then
; to `user`, so a namespaced file can construct a box.)

(ns dp)

(defprotocol Describe (describe ((self (ref Self))) i32))

(defstruct Fox n:i32)

(defn describe ((self (ref Fox))):i32 (return (+ 300 (_get self n))))

; Bare reference to this namespace's OWN protocol.
(extend Fox Describe)
